/// Initial selection policy when an idle text input first receives focus.
///
/// Pointer focus leaves placement and selection to the pointer gesture. A draft
/// retained across a blur also keeps its existing caret and selection.

/// Leave selected editing commands available to a containing component.
///
/// The editor still owns rendering and state; excluded commands are simply
/// omitted from this input's binding table so the owner can route them.

/// Resolve the field surface and text through another component's presentation.
/// Gutter, placeholder, marker, icon, and selection retain their own parts so
/// each can still be themed independently.

/// Resolve text decoration through another component's presentation.
///
/// The input keeps its text foreground and field surface. The host owns
/// the underline and underline modifier, while all auxiliary parts retain
/// their normal input theme. This is useful when the host owns a semantic
/// text state such as an inline editor's error underline.

/// Render this input as text embedded in a host-owned cell surface.
///
/// The input keeps its normal editing, selection, focus, and cursor
/// behavior while leaving the leading cell and focus indicator to its
/// host. One trailing cell remains reserved for a host marker.

/// Registers this Form input's keyboard stop without a pointer region.
///
/// Use only when Form layout clips the native input body. The native
/// disabled and read-only policy is preserved, including inherited Form
/// disabling.

/// Register this input's focus, pointer, and key-binding contract when a
/// host draws its own visible surface for the input state. The supplied
/// area must belong to the visible host control (for example, a searchable
/// list), not to an off-screen or hidden input. Unlike `draw`, this method
/// keeps the entire supplied host region for focus and pointer routing.

/// Geometry shared by TextArea drawing and coordinate-bearing input.
///
/// `window` describes the component body's visible rows. `text` is the
/// registered text part inside that body, so pointer, cursor and menu mapping
/// use the same physical origin and clipping bounds.

/// Project an active captured drag through the parent window. Unlike a
/// press, a captured drag remains meaningful after leaving `TEXT`; the
/// old logical child behavior extended to the document edge from the
/// captured origin. Clamp above the visible window to its first row, but
/// preserve vertical extrapolation below it so the caller can clamp to the
/// document edge rather than the parent's logical viewport.

/// Registers this Form text area's keyboard stop without a pointer region.
///
/// Use only when Form layout clips the native text area body. The native
/// disabled and read-only policy is preserved, including inherited Form
/// disabling.

/// Return the focused caret's source row inside this TextArea's logical
/// visible body, after the document's own scroll offset.
///
/// A containing Form can use this row to reveal the caret in its parent
/// viewport without reading or changing the document state.

/// Controls whether content-only fields size themselves from their view data.
///
/// `Fixed` preserves the original Form geometry. `Intrinsic` gives notes one
/// row per supplied line and gives choosers the rows their displayed value
/// needs. Other field kinds keep their existing sizing rules.

/// Sizes notes and chooser summaries from their supplied view data.
///
/// The default [`FieldSizingPolicy::Fixed`] preserves existing geometry.

/// Apply a borrowed semantic lane layout after checking its static shape
/// and field references. Active-group/data visibility completeness is
/// checked by [`Self::validate_layout`] before each rendering phase.

/// Keeps automatic reveal from moving a child hit target between pointer
/// press and release. The pointer-down intent starts the hold; release,
/// drag-end and cancellation end it. The snapshot's pressed flag is only
/// used to detect a gesture that became inactive without a terminal intent.

/// Estimates the legacy linear layout without consulting [`FormData`].
///
/// This compatibility method cannot account for data-dependent visibility,
/// radio option counts, or the row pairing used when `columns(2)` is set.
/// This estimate also ignores an explicit lane layout. Consumers with
/// form data or [`FieldSizingPolicy::Intrinsic`] should use
/// [`Self::measure_with_data`].

/// Measures the visible fields using the same placement plan as update and draw.
///
/// Measurement reads visibility and option data only. It does not update
/// controls, validate values, invoke domain handlers, or mutate form state.

/// Measures with explicit design tokens so composed overlays can use the
/// same placement policy before a [`Ui`] draw pass exists.
///
/// This is crate-visible; consumers should use [`Self::measure_with_data`].

/// Persistent state for one form dialog.
///
/// Field values remain owned by the caller's [`FormData`]. This state only
/// contains the existing form editing/scroll state and dialog lifecycle state.

/// Reusable modal form. Field behavior and the action row are delegated to
/// [`Form`]; title, chrome, layer scope, and dismissal are delegated to
/// [`Dialog`].

/// Sets how Enter behaves when a form field is not editing.
///
/// The default submits, matching [`Form`]. Use [`EnterPolicy::Never`] when
/// the caller handles submission through a separate scoped command.

/// Submits the current native form values after a scoped command bubbles
